/* QuickTerm — English (base) UI strings for Menus.
 *
 * ONE AREA = ONE TABLE. Every `<Area>.strings` inside a `.lproj` is loaded and merged at
 * runtime, so separate translation passes add their own file instead of all appending to one
 * shared table. A key declared in two tables fails LocalizationTests.
 *
 * English is the development language: every key MUST exist here, and any key missing from
 * another language falls back to this table (never to the raw key).
 *
 * A NEW table file (Panes.strings, StatusBar.strings …) must be added to BOTH .lproj folders
 * and then `xcodegen generate` re-run — this project is generated from project.yml, and a
 * table that is not in the project is simply never copied into the app bundle. The build
 * refuses it (scripts/check-localization.py) rather than letting the app draw raw keys.
 *
 * Rules (enforced on every build by scripts/check-localization.py, and by
 * Tests/LocalizationTests.swift):
 *   - one key = one WHOLE sentence or one whole label; never a fragment that code glues together;
 *   - the only format specifier is %1$@, %2$@ … (positional). Never %@, %d, %f. A literal
 *     percent sign is written %%;
 *   - a key that varies with a count comes as a ".one"/".other" pair, read through Lp(_:count:_:);
 *   - keys are lowercase, dot separated, area first: <area>.<subject>.<detail>.
 *
 * Not localized, by policy: the quickterm CLI, OSLog messages, wire identifiers, config keys,
 * pane handles, and the AppKit "undo"/"redo" selector names.
 */

